menu "ESP32 Wi-Fi starter"

    config APP_ENABLE_WIFI_RADIO
        bool "Enable the Wi-Fi radio (STA join + SoftAP configuration portal)"
        default y
        help
            Enable the real Wi-Fi radio. Keep this ON for physical hardware:
            the device joins the stored network as a station and, when no
            credentials are available, starts the "ESP32-Setup" SoftAP so the
            user can configure it.

            Turn this OFF for the ESP-IDF QEMU emulator, which does not emulate
            the Wi-Fi radio (bringing it up panics). With the radio disabled the
            firmware serves the exact same configuration web portal over the
            emulated Ethernet interface, so the interface can be exercised end
            to end in emulation. See sdkconfig.qemu.

endmenu
